# The preset policy in kgsm-base decides which of this host's kgsm units run; applying it is
# symlink manipulation on disk, so it works during the transaction and in a chroot alike. Starting
# anything is the node's post-transaction hook's job, which is where a running system is available.
#
# post_install only. An administrator who disabled the timer keeps it disabled across every later
# version — re-presetting on upgrade would quietly undo that.

post_install() {
    systemctl preset kgsm-journal-prune.timer >/dev/null 2>&1 || true

    cat <<'MSG'

  The engine is installed at /opt/kgsm, on PATH as /usr/bin/kgsm.

  Instances, blueprints and overrides live under the kgsm account's XDG paths and survive every
  upgrade. Nothing here needs configuring before the engine works.

  Native instances are supervised by kgsm-watchdog. Without it kgsm spawns a game directly and run
  state is unreliable, so install it unless this host runs container instances only.

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'MSG'

  If pacman wrote a .pacnew beside a file under /etc, merge it. The engine's own config is under
  the kgsm account's home and is migrated in place on the next run.

MSG
}
